# Everything here is optional, and commented out on purpose: a service with a URL
# but no key shows up as broken on the dashboard. You do not need this file to
# use Wheelhouse. Create the administrator on first run, then add your services
# under Admin, Services (keys are stored encrypted). Variables below are a
# read-only alternative that keeps working for existing installations; an
# instance saved in the app wins over the same id here. The full list, with
# defaults, is in the README ("Configuration").
#
# Remove the leading "# " and fill in BOTH the URL and the key of each service
# you want. Sonarr/Radarr power the Library, Explore and Codecs pages.
# SONARR_URL=http://localhost:8989
# SONARR_API_KEY=
#
# RADARR_URL=http://localhost:7878
# RADARR_API_KEY=

# More than one Radarr or Sonarr: RADARR_<ID>_URL and RADARR_<ID>_API_KEY.
# RADARR_4K_* becomes the instance "radarr-4k", shown as "Radarr 4K".
# RADARR_4K_URL=http://localhost:7879
# RADARR_4K_API_KEY=

# SABnzbd and/or qBittorrent (v4 or v5; all three qBittorrent values are needed).
# SABNZBD_URL=http://localhost:8080
# SABNZBD_API_KEY=
# QBITTORRENT_URL=http://localhost:8081
# QBITTORRENT_USERNAME=admin
# QBITTORRENT_PASSWORD=

# Media server status cards. Plex, Jellyfin or both. The Jellyfin key is made
# in Jellyfin under Dashboard -> API Keys.
# PLEX_URL=http://localhost:32400
# PLEX_TOKEN=
# JELLYFIN_URL=http://localhost:8096
# JELLYFIN_API_KEY=

# Powers Explore (with Radarr). Free key from themoviedb.org (account settings
# -> API). TMDB_BASE_URL overrides the API root, for a caching proxy; leave unset.
# TMDB_API_KEY=
# TMDB_BASE_URL=

# Server settings (the container image already sets PORT=3050).
# Listen on one address instead of all interfaces (overrides PORT). HOSTNAME is
# never used, so a container runtime setting it cannot break the listen address.
# WHEELHOUSE_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:3050
# Folders Convert may touch, separated like PATH (default /movies:/tv).
# WHEELHOUSE_MEDIA_ROOTS=/movies:/tv
# Reverse proxies whose X-Forwarded-* headers are believed (operations.md).
# WHEELHOUSE_TRUSTED_PROXIES=
# Host names that may use the local-network bypass, besides IP addresses,
# localhost and single-label names (operations.md).
# WHEELHOUSE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
